    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "Use the same instructions at every step. For λx.λy.x, start at level 0 and carry 0 through both bodies, so x sits at level 0. For λx.f (g x), carry 0 into the body, give the outer function f level 0, and give its argument g x level 1. Apply the rule again inside that argument: g stays at 1, and x lands at 2.",
